<title>USA: U.S. supports broad objectives of EMU - Tyson.</title>
<headline>U.S. supports broad objectives of EMU - Tyson.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>White House economist Laura Tyson said the United States supported the broad objectives of Europe's efforts to achieve monetary union.</p>
<p>&quot;We support clearly the broad objectives of EMU and we want to make sure there is a strong foundation in place for its development,&quot; Tyson said in response to a question at a breakfast organized by Reuters.  </p>
<p>Tyson said European monetary union would clearly be a major change in the global economy and global financial system.</p>
<p>She said it would be important for European leaders to make sure the implications of this change were well understood &quot;and that we take whatever action is required to keep the stability of the global fianancial system which is so important to global prosperity.&quot;</p>
</text>
